       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 50 mg of amlodipine daily has no therapeutic use. It is well above the 10 mg maximum, and this patient has normal kidney and liver function, so nothing would justify it. Entering it risks serious harm: profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema that could last for days.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily.** Tell me which one and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Help you with an uncontrolled-BP plan.** Uptitrating to 10 mg and adding a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, is the standard approach. I can enter those orders.\n- **Route this to pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason for the dose that I don't know about, please talk with the pharmacist or the attending first. They can place the order through their own channels if they agree.\n\nWhich would you like?"
